# mcp-remote Configuration Examples

## Custom Authorization Header with Environment Variable

Here's how to configure Claude Desktop with a custom Authorization header while avoiding the Windows escaping bug:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "remote-example": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "mcp-remote",
        "https://remote.mcp.server/sse",
        "--header",
        "Authorization:${AUTH_HEADER}"
      ],
      "env": {
        "AUTH_HEADER": "Bearer your-token-here"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The documentation notes: **"Cursor, Codex-Cli and Claude Desktop (Windows) have a bug where spaces inside `args` aren't escaped when it invokes `npx`, which ends up mangling these values."** By removing spaces around the colon and placing the actual token value in an environment variable, the configuration works correctly across platforms.

## Allowing HTTP Connections

To connect to internal services using HTTP (non-HTTPS) in trusted private networks:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "internal-service": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "mcp-remote",
        "http://internal-service.vpc/sse",
        "--allow-http"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Per the documentation: **"This should only be used in secure private networks where traffic cannot be intercepted."**

